1
00:00:00,396 --> 00:00:04,857
TutorLoop is the back office for student
tutors. It was built by Aariv Patel,

2
00:00:04,877 --> 00:00:06,458
a high schooler near Houston.

3
00:00:08,624 --> 00:00:13,701
Lots of students tutor younger kids, and they run it
out of a notes app and a Venmo feed.

4
00:00:13,721 --> 00:00:14,506
Three things break.

5
00:00:14,881 --> 00:00:21,082
Money: after a few weeks, nobody remembers who paid.
Parents: families want to know if tutoring is working.

6
00:00:21,102 --> 00:00:26,958
And proof: volunteer tutoring counts toward NHS service hours,
which need a log a sponsor can sign.

7
00:00:27,332 --> 00:00:31,558
Tutoring software exists, but it's built
for companies with staff and budgets,

8
00:00:31,578 --> 00:00:34,743
not a sixteen-year-old with three students. That's the gap.

9
00:00:35,736 --> 00:00:38,874
Here's the live app, brand new. Type one student, the minutes,

10
00:00:38,894 --> 00:00:40,883
what you covered, and how it went.

11
00:00:44,349 --> 00:00:48,240
Save, and TutorLoop has already drafted
the parent update and the invoice.

12
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:50,848
That's the whole idea in about thirty seconds.

13
00:00:52,315 --> 00:00:57,432
Now load sample data to show a busy month. A
bar at the top says the students are made up.

14
00:00:57,804 --> 00:01:04,630
One glance shows this month's earnings, $115 still
unpaid, and 2.25 of 10 service hours.

15
00:01:05,001 --> 00:01:10,698
Ethan's family owes $90. Remind writes a
polite, itemized email with both session dates.

16
00:01:14,334 --> 00:01:18,618
Logging a session takes about ten seconds:
student, minutes, topics, a quick note.

17
00:01:18,638 --> 00:01:20,936
It previews the amount as you type.

18
00:01:23,181 --> 00:01:25,088
Save, and any action can be undone.

19
00:01:26,784 --> 00:01:33,116
Parent updates are the part families notice. TutorLoop reads
the tutor's own session notes and writes the update:

20
00:01:33,136 --> 00:01:36,999
topics, the trend, the latest win, what's next, and the balance.

21
00:01:37,370 --> 00:01:39,695
Edit it, then one click opens it in your email.

22
00:01:41,837 --> 00:01:46,315
Unpaid sessions roll into an invoice. At
month's end there's one statement per family,

23
00:01:46,335 --> 00:01:48,243
or one recap for a sponsor.

24
00:01:50,367 --> 00:01:57,856
Volunteer sessions count toward a goal and export as a CSV or
a printable log with a signature line for the NHS sponsor.

25
00:01:59,983 --> 00:02:03,380
Free covers three students and the whole product. At the limit,

26
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:07,108
TutorLoop shows the plans and prices
Pro in the tutor's own terms:

27
00:02:07,128 --> 00:02:10,525
about nine minutes of tutoring a month. Checkout is a demo;

28
00:02:10,545 --> 00:02:11,457
no money moves.

29
00:02:12,914 --> 00:02:17,408
Under the hood it's plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. No framework,

30
00:02:17,428 --> 00:02:19,460
no server, no paid APIs.

31
00:02:24,154 --> 00:02:28,504
core.js is pure business logic: money in cents, balances, invoices, summaries,

32
00:02:28,524 --> 00:02:35,258
and the report engine. It never touches the page,
so it runs in Node with unit tests.

33
00:02:45,783 --> 00:02:51,195
Today's run: 65 unit tests, 11 money
property tests, and 66 DOM checks,

34
00:02:51,215 --> 00:02:58,716
all passing. A strict content security policy blocks inline
scripts, and a service worker makes it work offline.

35
00:03:03,065 --> 00:03:06,838
Parent updates come from an on-device
engine. It costs nothing per report,

36
00:03:06,858 --> 00:03:09,367
and notes about kids never leave the device.

37
00:03:14,385 --> 00:03:21,072
Scaling is cheap by design. Static files on a CDN
cost the same for ten tutors or a hundred thousand,

38
00:03:21,092 --> 00:03:25,097
and a test runs five thousand
sessions under a strict time budget.

39
00:03:25,117 --> 00:03:29,121
For Pro sync, the data maps
onto Postgres tables with row-level security.

40
00:03:30,578 --> 00:03:35,148
The business model is freemium: free for
three students, Pro at $4 a month,

41
00:03:35,168 --> 00:03:40,066
and Club at $99 a school year, so
one NHS sponsor brings a whole chapter.

42
00:03:40,436 --> 00:03:44,812
NHS has more than 16,000 chapters.
If every one paid for Club,

43
00:03:44,832 --> 00:03:49,209
that's a ceiling of about $1.5
million a year. It's a ceiling,

44
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:50,308
not a forecast.

45
00:03:50,679 --> 00:03:56,787
Today there are no users or revenue yet. Next is
a pilot with student tutors and one NHS sponsor.

46
00:03:57,847 --> 00:04:02,135
That's TutorLoop. It's free at aariv.me/Tutorloop. Thanks for watching.

